"Internal Error ()\nciteturn10view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://doi.org/10.1057/jos.2012.20\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://doi.org/10.1057/jos.2012.20: (403) Forbidden--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn10view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2007.00593.x\",\"lineno\":null}); \nURL https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2007.00593.x is not accessible via this tool.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2204.11890] Simulating key properties of lithium-ion batteries with a fault-tolerant quantum computer (https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11890)\nciteturn10view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.11890\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 166\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Quantum Physics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 25 Apr 2022 (【5†v1】), last revised 6 Feb 2023 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Simulating key properties of lithium-ion batteries with a fault-tolerant quantum computer\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【6†Alain Delgado】, 【7†Pablo A. M. Casares】, 【8†Roberto dos Reis】, 【9†Modjtaba Shokrian Zini】, 【10†Roberto Campos】, 【11†Norge Cruz-Hernández】, 【12†Arne-Christian Voigt】, 【13†Angus Lowe】, 【14†Soran Jahangiri】, 【15†M. A. Martin-Delgado】, 【16†Jonathan E. Mueller】, 【17†Juan Miguel Arrazola】\nL12: View a PDF of the paper titled Simulating key properties of lithium-ion batteries with a fault-tolerant quantum computer, by Alain Delgado and 11 other authors\nL13: \nL14: 【18†View PDF】 【19†HTML (experimental)】\nL15: > Abstract:There is a pressing need to develop new rechargeable battery technologies that can offer higher energy storage, faster charging, and lower costs. Despite the success of existing methods for the simulation of battery materials, they can sometimes fall short of delivering accurate and reliable results. Quantum computing has been discussed as an avenue to overcome these issues, but only limited work has been done to outline how they may impact battery simulations.\nL16: In this work, we provide a detailed answer to the following question: how can a quantum computer be used to simulate key properties of a lithium-ion battery? Based on recently-introduced first-quantization techniques, we lay out an end-to-end quantum algorithm for calculating equilibrium cell voltages, ionic mobility, and thermal stability.\nL17: These can be obtained from ground-state energies of materials, which is the core calculation executed by the quantum computer using qubitization-based quantum phase estimation. The algorithm includes explicit methods for preparing approximate ground states of periodic materials in first quantization. We bring these insights together to perform the first estimation of the resources required to implement a quantum algorithm for simulating a realistic cathode material, dilithium iron silicate.\nL18: Comments:  | 31 pages, 14 figures\nL19: Subjects:  | Quantum Physics (quant-ph); Materials Science (cond-mat.mtrl-sci)\nL20: Cite as:  | 【20†arXiv:2204.11890】 [quant-ph]\nL21:    | (or 【21†arXiv:2204.11890v2】 [quant-ph] for this version)\nL22:    | 【22†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2204.11890†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: Journal reference:  | Phys. Rev. A 106, 032428 (2022)\nL24: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | 【23†https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.106.032428†doi.org】 DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Alain Delgado Gran [【24†view email】]\nL28: 【5†[v1]】 Mon, 25 Apr 2022 18:01:04 UTC (1,688 KB)\nL29: [v2] Mon, 6 Feb 2023 18:37:37 UTC (1,690 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: 